WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.187
Why can an agent loop forever?

00:00:02.187 --> 00:00:05.532
One common cause is an impossible grader.

00:00:05.532 --> 00:00:14.387
Suppose retrieval repeatedly returns useful policy text, but the grader is so strict that it rejects every document.

00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:18.735
The graph keeps rewriting and retrieving until it reaches the limit.

00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:27.284
Before redesigning the graph, log the current query, returned source I D's, grade, threshold, selected route,

00:00:27.284 --> 00:00:35.009
and step count. If useful evidence is always rejected, fix the grading policy.

00:00:35.009 --> 00:00:43.715
If the rewrite barely changes the query and the same chunks return, detect no progress and stop or change strategy.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.957
The graph may be working exactly as written.

00:00:46.957 --> 00:00:49.734
The problem can be the decision rule inside it.
